From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: take the edge weight at the first opportunity

rcpi_at_start was NULL on five edges out of six.

Not a broken join: an edge is recorded the moment it appears, and at that
moment the child bSTA has usually not been measured yet - it has just
associated. The signal arrives seconds later, by which time the row is
already written.

So the snapshot is taken at the first opportunity instead of only at the
first instant. While the edge is still open and the weight is still unknown,
the next sync that has a real signal writes it; once written it is never
revised, because the column records what the choice looked like, not how the
link behaved afterwards - that is metric_hist.

Still NULL when nothing is known. A column that is sometimes NULL is a
nuisance; a column filled with zeros that read as measurements is the defect
this whole series of patches has been closing.

Verify: after a re-parent, the new row may be NULL for a few seconds and must
then carry a plausible rcpi - and must never become 0.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -931,6 +931,40 @@
 			mapdb_bind_int(st, 1, now_ts);
 			stmt_finish(c->db, st);
 		}
+
+		/* Fill in the weight once it exists.
+		 *
+		 * An edge is recorded the moment it appears, and at that moment
+		 * the child's bSTA has usually not been measured yet - it has
+		 * just associated. Measured after the first deploy: one edge of
+		 * six carried a value, five were NULL.
+		 *
+		 * So the snapshot is taken at the first opportunity rather than
+		 * only at the first instant: while the edge is still open and
+		 * the weight is still unknown, the next sync that has a real
+		 * signal writes it. Once written it is never revised - it is
+		 * meant to record what the choice looked like, not to follow
+		 * the link afterwards. That is metric_hist's job.
+		 *
+		 * Left NULL when nothing is known. A column that is mostly NULL
+		 * is a nuisance; a column filled with zeros that read as
+		 * measurements is a defect. */
+		static const char *weigh_sql =
+			"UPDATE topology_link_history SET rcpi_at_start = ("
+			"  SELECT s.rcpi FROM sta s"
+			"    JOIN bstamld b ON b.mld_macaddr = s.macaddr"
+			"   WHERE b.agent_almac = topology_link_history.child_almac"
+			"     AND s.rcpi BETWEEN 1 AND 254 LIMIT 1) "
+			"WHERE to_ts IS NULL AND rcpi_at_start IS NULL "
+			"  AND EXISTS ("
+			"  SELECT 1 FROM sta s"
+			"    JOIN bstamld b ON b.mld_macaddr = s.macaddr"
+			"   WHERE b.agent_almac = topology_link_history.child_almac"
+			"     AND s.rcpi BETWEEN 1 AND 254)";
+
+		st = NULL;
+		if (mapdb_prepare(c->db, weigh_sql, &st) == MAPDB_OK)
+			stmt_finish(c->db, st);
 	}
 
 	/* Fold the backhaul signal into the hourly series.
